# Boards are user data, not source. Keep test boards out of the repo.
*.mbrd

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Installed agent skills, and the lockfile that records where they came from.
# Ignored rather than committed because a skill installer writes two mirrored
# trees - .agents/skills/ and .claude/skills/ - and eighty files of somebody
# else's prose rode into this repository that way once already. They are a
# property of a working copy and not of the project: nothing here builds, tests
# or lints from them. The one that mattered is vendored on purpose instead,
# byte for byte, at tools/oxlint/anti-slop, which is the copy .oxlintrc.json
# loads and the only one that has ever run.
.agents/
.claude/skills/
skills-lock.json

# The desktop shell. Its sources are committed; none of this is. dist/ is the
# two esbuild bundles, out/ is electron-builder's installers, and resources/
# holds the per-platform ffmpeg binary a script fetches at release time - 80-odd
# megabytes that belong to a release rather than to a repository.
desktop/node_modules/
desktop/dist/
desktop/out/
desktop/resources/ffmpeg/
desktop/test-results/
desktop/playwright-report/

# The portable copy. `npm run portable` writes it: the unpacked application plus
# the `portable` marker installer.nsh's Portable branch writes, which is the
# whole of what a portable copy is. portable/data/ inside it is boards and is
# survived by a rebuild - see desktop/scripts/portable.mjs. It sat at the
# repository root until the root was cleared of everything that had a choice.
desktop/portable/

# Node. The app has no dependencies; these are the two optional dev tools -
# `npm run lint` and `npm run typecheck`. `npm test` needs neither, and needs
# no install at all.
node_modules/

# Tool output: code-graph dumps, including session transcripts.
graphify-out/

# Editor and tooling scratch. Here because one did get committed: a 30KB
# ui/fonts.ts.bak rode into a commit on a `git add -A` during the TypeScript
# conversion, and nothing would have caught it - a stray copy of a real module
# is not a syntax error, no test walks for it, and it reads as a file somebody
# meant to keep. The rule is cheaper than the vigilance.
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# The dev bundle's source map. `npm run dev` writes it and devtools reads it;
# `npm run build` does not emit one at all, so nothing that ships refers to it.
# Ignored rather than committed because it is 2.9MB that changes on every build,
# which is a repository growing by a browser convenience nobody reviews. The
# sources themselves still ship beside the bundle, so the deployed app is still
# readable - one step further away than it was, which is the trade the bundle
# was costed at.
web/assets/app.js.map

# Local tunnel binary - a 52MB vendored exe, not source.
cloudflared.exe

# Wrangler's scratch directory. The deploy config itself (wrangler.jsonc) is
# source and is committed; this is the cache it writes beside it.
.wrangler/
